18.text:
PRIVATE REFLECTION: {Core NI 45-106 tests (Jan 2021) unchanged: individuals via income (>200k solo/>300k joint, 2 prior yrs + expectation), net fin assets >1M, or net assets >=5M (solo/joint); non-individual entities via own net assets >=5M on latest FS OR all interest owners themselves AIs.

Round-0 split (A vs E) has shifted sharply: 9+ colleagues now converge on A (majority view: LP itself shows no >=5M FS net assets; "all owners AIs" route blocked because GP holding co's qualification rests solely on gifted $6M cash with no FS or enumerated test proof). E remains minority contender (Alex/Bob individually fail; GIC-liab math yields ~5.2M but unknown investment-property values/FS prevent confirming entity test).

D arguments (minority) hinge on James's non-AI status blocking "all owners" with no independent entity net-assets shown. B/C claims largely refuted by income/net-assets numbers. Unresolved tension: whether gifted assets alone establish GP's FS net-assets test; no look-through or other exemptions alter facts. Current evidence favors A as only structure failing both entity limbs without additional assumptions.}

